  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 336 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nThe upper level ridging builds northward from the Southern Plains \nagain Friday into the weekend. This will bring a return to hot \ntemperatures, with some areas likely pushing advisory criteria, with \ntemperatures above 100 degrees. By early next week, the ridge sinks \nback across the southern plains. This will allow for a return of \nseveral disturbances rotating around the high. Moisture content will \nremain high as sub-tropical moisture continues rotate north and then \neastward across the region. This will likely lead to an increase in \nshowers and thunderstorms once again along with a slight cooling\ntrend in temperatures.",
